    "title": "",
    "legend": "Aspirated material displays malignant epithelial cells arranged individually or in loosely cohesive tissue fragments. The malignant cells are characterized by their large size; their hyperchromatic nuclei with prominent nucleoli; and their abundant, finely vacuolated to clear cytoplasm. The mucinous cells contain large amounts of intracytoplasmic mucin. Scattered ciliated respiratory epithelial cells and lymphocytes are seen in the background (Pap).",
