    "title": "<p>Salivary gland&ndash;type carcinomas: ancillary testing</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Marianne Engels",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 697.65pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" color: black; \">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" color: black; \">Immunocytochemistry</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" color: black; \">Molecular pathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 1.25pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" \">Mucoepidermoid carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" \">All cell types: CK7+, TTF1&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" \">Mucous cells: MUC5AC+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" \">Intermediate and squamous cells: CK5/6+, p40+, p63+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{24743219; 28484699; 26575266}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"\"><span style=\" \">CRTC1</span></em><span style=\" \">::<em style=\"\">MAML2</em> gene fusion (FISH or NGS) present in the majority of cases </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{24743219; 26575266; 28343305}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 1.25pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" color: black; \">Adenoid cystic carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" color: black; \">Myoepithelial/basal cells: p63+, S100+, SMA+, calponin+, vimentin+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" color: black; \">Luminal cells: CK7+, EMA+, CK5/6+, KIT&nbsp;(CD117)+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{33776449; 31343850; 28484699}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"\"><span style=\" color: black; \">MYB</span></em><span style=\" color: black; \">::<em style=\"\">NFIB</em> or <em>MYBL1</em>::<em style=\"\">NFIB</em> gene fusion (FISH or NGS) present in most cases (small series) </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{33776449; 31028361}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" height: 1.25pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\" \">Epithelial-myoepithelial carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" \">Epithelial cells: CK7+, cytokeratin AE1/AE3+, MNF116+, SOX10+, EMA+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\" \">Myoepithelial cells: CK5/6+, p40+, p63+, S100+, calponin, SOX10+, SMA+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{27583848; 11353064}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 299.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"399\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"\"><span style=\" \">PLAG1</span></em><span style=\" \"> and <em style=\"\">HMGA2</em> rearrangements/amplifications (FISH) </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{29135520; 25439740}</span></span><span style=\" \">: <em style=\"\">PLAG1</em> in 23% of cases, <em style=\"\">HMGA2</em> in 26% of cases</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"\"><span style=\" \">CTNNB1</span></em><span style=\" \"> and <em style=\"\">FGFR1</em> rearrangements </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{25439740}</span></span><span style=\" \"> in rare cases (FISH)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em style=\"\"><span style=\" \">HRAS</span></em><span style=\" \"> codon&nbsp;61 mutations </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\" \">{24277618; 30994537}</span></span><span style=\" \"> present in ~80% of cases</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">NGS, next-generation sequencing; TTF1, thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1.</p>",
